   "title": "Application block diagram: half-bridge converter",
   "page": 3,
   "description": "A PWM controller on +12 V drives HI and LI; the HIP2100 runs from the same +12 V on VDD with a bypass capacitor to ground, and switches a half bridge of two N-channel MOSFETs across a +100 V bus. HO drives the upper FET, whose source is the switch node tied to HS; LO drives the lower FET, source to ground. The bootstrap capacitor sits between HB and HS and is charged through the on-chip diode from VDD. Two series capacitors split the bus; the transformer primary runs from their midpoint to the switch node. The secondary feeds the secondary circuit, whose feedback returns to the controller through a reference and isolation stage referred to the secondary ground.",
